    "problem": "Infinite Horizon Markov Economies In this paper, we study a generalization of Markov games and pseudo-games that we call Markov pseudo-games, which, like the former, captures time and uncertainty, and like the latter, allows for the players' actions to determine the set of actions available to the other players. In the same vein as Arrow and Debreu, we intend for this model to be rich enough to\u2026",
